Build 1.2.7 - 2026-08-16 - THE APP GETS ITS COMPOSER, AND THE WALL IS REBUILT

Cut from main after everything the owner reported in a four-hour session on his
phone. Verified against ORIGIN, not a local copy: the branch was reset to what
is actually on GitHub and re-run from there.

  typecheck 0 · 1,841 tests pass · production build 0
  92 screenshots, ZERO real problems (web, 360, 390, desktop AND app mode)

VERSION IS 1.2.7. Build #93 already carried 1.2.6 and this is different code.
Two artefacts sharing a version string is how the Play Console, the crash
reports and the About screen stop agreeing with each other.

THE ROOT CAUSE OF EVERYTHING BELOW

The screenshot checker had NEVER ONCE rendered the app. `isNativeCapacitorApp()`
reads `window.Capacitor`, nothing in the harness ever set it, so every one of
the 63 screenshots it had been passing was the WEBSITE. It reported "0 problems"
the same morning the owner found three real faults on his phone in two minutes.

That is fixed first and permanently: there is now an `app-360` viewport, and the
wall and the visitor-view of a wall have their own scenes. A checker that
silently tests half the product is worse than none, because it issues a clean
bill of health for the half it never opened.

WHAT THE OWNER REPORTED, AND WHAT WAS DONE

 1. THE COMPOSER. Picking a photo on the app went straight to a 160x160
    thumbnail — no Crop, no cover choice, no reorder, no sight of the framing.
    On a photography platform, on the device nearly everyone posts from.
    It now renders the SAME composer component the website does. Not a copy.

 2. THE BLANK GAP IN THE FEED. An empty advert slot returns nothing for a
    normal member but drew an ADMIN placeholder for an admin — which he is —
    and that placeholder inherited the story-card frame: full-bleed at 4:5,
    reserving about 450px for two words of grey text. Now a compact strip.
    No member ever saw this. Only he did.

 3. THE WALL. Rebuilt against his Instagram reference, measured off the
    screenshot rather than eyeballed: name over the counts, kebab top-right,
    white bio, thin "+" story rings, icon-only tabs with a white underline,
    4:5 tiles that TOUCH, and ONE 18px left edge for the whole screen where
    there had been four different ones.

 4. TOP BAR. The three icons were 20/16/16px — three sizes in one row. All
    24px now, in 44x44 targets, with the Create and Search glyphs measured to
    26px from their respective edges.

 5. GRID COUNTS. Likes and comments on wall tiles were hover-only, so on a
    phone they did not exist at all. First tap reveals, second opens — his own
    rule from 14 August, which I had applied to the feed and written the
    opposite of into the grid.

THREE HE NEVER SAW, all shipping, all found by photographing the app:

  · AN INFINITE RENDER LOOP on every profile — "Maximum update depth exceeded",
    four times per page load, burning battery for as long as the page was open.
    `extData?.entries || []` built a new array every render and was a
    dependency of an effect that called setState. Verified 4 before, 0 after.
  · a long name rendering UNDERNEATH the ⋮ menu.
  · "mutual friends" printing with NO NUMBER in front of it.

WHAT TO CHECK ON THE PHONE - only your device can answer these

  1. POST A PHOTO. After picking, you must now get the full composer: the photo
     at publishing size, the thirds guide, Crop, the Cover badge, reorder. This
     is the change. A source test pins the wiring, but no test here can drive a
     native gallery — this one needs your thumb.
  2. Your wall: one straight left edge down the whole screen, photos touching.
  3. Tap a wall photo ONCE — the like/comment counts appear. Tap again — it opens.
  4. Open somebody else's profile: Follow and Message should look like buttons,
     not tiny uppercase links.
  5. Scroll the feed: no blank hole between posts any more.

NOT DONE, AND NOT CLAIMED

 - his reference has four content tabs; ours has two. NO REELS, ever.
 - `svgo` is still absent from both lockfiles, so SVGs ship unoptimised.
   Pre-existing, unrelated, deliberately not touched beside a build.
 - the harness has no fixtures for the Works tab, so those scenes log missing
   data. Test scaffolding, not an app fault.

Then promote the AAB.
